WEBVTT

00:01.376 --> 00:03.211
EPISODE TWO
AND NOW... I'M GOING TO MOVE THE EARTH

00:03.294 --> 00:05.296
If it's the Earth that moves,

00:05.880 --> 00:08.133
reason and beauty become one.

00:10.510 --> 00:14.431
The cosmos is unified
under a single order.

00:15.849 --> 00:19.644
If the theory accepted
by the Church is the geocentric model,

00:21.062 --> 00:23.898
mine is heliocentrism. How about that?

00:26.484 --> 00:29.195
Helio... centrism?

00:29.904 --> 00:32.365
S-Such an idea...

00:34.743 --> 00:35.577
could...

00:36.661 --> 00:37.495
No.

00:39.789 --> 00:41.958
That's just plain wrong.

00:43.918 --> 00:45.712
I'll give you three reasons.

00:48.298 --> 00:51.134
First, there are too many contradictions.

00:51.634 --> 00:54.137
If the Earth is moving...

00:57.348 --> 01:00.769
why do I land in the same spot
when I jump?

01:02.312 --> 01:03.396
Second.

01:03.480 --> 01:05.899
If we accept that the Earth is moving,

01:05.982 --> 01:07.609
who would support that theory?

01:08.318 --> 01:10.695
The Earth is at the center of the universe

01:10.779 --> 01:14.449
because God wanted
humankind's home to be special.

01:15.116 --> 01:17.577
To deny that would be disastrous.

01:19.662 --> 01:20.872
And third.

01:21.372 --> 01:23.750
Risking your life for intuition

01:24.334 --> 01:25.627
is foolish.

01:27.212 --> 01:28.630
A sound argument.

01:29.255 --> 01:31.549
However, I disagree with your third point.

01:33.718 --> 01:36.805
It's because my life is on the line

01:36.888 --> 01:38.348
that I believe my intuition.

01:40.767 --> 01:43.394
And what if you're wrong?

01:44.854 --> 01:45.939
It doesn't matter.

01:46.564 --> 01:48.983
A wrong answer is not a meaningless one.

01:49.984 --> 01:52.821
"A wrong answer is not a meaningless one"?

01:53.571 --> 01:55.156
Are you insane?

01:55.240 --> 01:58.660
I don't find
your heliocentric theory beautiful,

01:58.743 --> 02:01.663
nor will I jump through fire to prove it.

02:03.623 --> 02:05.458
I don't want to come here tomorrow.

02:05.959 --> 02:06.793
Is that so?

02:08.545 --> 02:09.420
Huh?

02:09.504 --> 02:12.173
I'll see you tomorrow then.

02:22.058 --> 02:25.019
<i>The heavens are still,
and the Earth moves?</i>

02:25.520 --> 02:29.774
<i>Not only that,
but it rotates and revolves too?</i>

02:31.526 --> 02:34.154
<i>How could something
that ridiculous be true?</i>

02:36.489 --> 02:37.323
<i>Just look.</i>

02:37.407 --> 02:40.660
<i>Even now, the stars are moving
in small increments.</i>

02:41.911 --> 02:44.122
<i>Watch for an hour, and it's clear.</i>

02:45.290 --> 02:47.458
<i>Even the idea of rotation is impossible.</i>

02:57.177 --> 02:59.095
Man, that hurt!

02:59.179 --> 03:00.889
How clumsy of me.

03:02.140 --> 03:05.101
I thought the mountains
flipped over for a second.

03:09.689 --> 03:11.774
The mountains flipped over?

03:13.651 --> 03:15.945
<i>B-But that's only because</i>

03:16.029 --> 03:17.739
<i>I was moving.</i>

03:17.822 --> 03:20.200
<i>It's not the mountains that moved.</i>

03:22.118 --> 03:23.995
<i>That much is obvious.</i>

03:24.704 --> 03:27.832
<i>But if I extend that obvious logic...</i>

03:31.794 --> 03:35.256
<i>If I'm the Earth,
and the mountains are the Sun...</i>

03:36.549 --> 03:38.343
<i>If the observer moves...</i>

03:40.428 --> 03:42.180
<i>the still object in the distance</i>

03:42.680 --> 03:44.724
<i>will also appear to move.</i>

03:51.022 --> 03:53.691
It may... be rotating.

03:54.192 --> 03:55.777
<i>No, wait!</i>

03:56.736 --> 03:59.197
Even if I accepted the rotation...

04:01.491 --> 04:03.534
there's no way it's revolving.

04:04.035 --> 04:07.205
<i>Let's say Earth moves
for the sake of argument.</i>

04:07.914 --> 04:11.292
<i>I'll apply Ptolemy's model
to the heliocentric theory.</i>

04:11.793 --> 04:14.963
<i>I just need to expand
or shrink the epicyclical radius</i>

04:15.046 --> 04:18.466
<i>of the planets thought to be
beyond the Sun to equal the radius</i>

04:18.549 --> 04:20.718
<i>of the current Sun's revolution.</i>

04:20.802 --> 04:23.012
<i>For planets closer than the Sun,</i>

04:23.096 --> 04:25.723
<i>I'll expand the center
of their epicycles to equal the Sun.</i>

04:25.807 --> 04:29.143
<i>If their induction path
is the same as the current Sun's orbit,</i>

04:29.227 --> 04:33.648
<i>and the Earth followed the same path
as it revolved around the Sun...</i>

04:36.943 --> 04:39.654
<i>This is ridiculous blasphemy.</i>

04:39.737 --> 04:41.364
<i>It's nonsense and plain wrong.</i>

04:42.198 --> 04:44.534
<i>Not only that, I could be arrested.</i>

04:44.617 --> 04:46.327
<i>I have no reason to pursue it.</i>

04:47.620 --> 04:50.581
<i>The individual planets move in sequence,</i>

04:51.207 --> 04:54.085
<i>and the cosmos is unified
under a single order.</i>

04:54.669 --> 04:57.130
<i>Everything moves in a harmonious sequence?</i>

04:57.630 --> 05:01.301
<i>The entire universe moves
under a single order?</i>

05:04.387 --> 05:05.555
<i>It's all lies!</i>

05:05.638 --> 05:08.099
<i>The planets move independently.</i>

05:09.976 --> 05:11.144
<i>That has to be it.</i>

05:11.227 --> 05:12.145
<i>Because if not...</i>

05:14.605 --> 05:16.607
<i>If the vastness of heaven</i>

05:16.691 --> 05:18.276
<i>moved with one mind</i>

05:18.901 --> 05:21.321
<i>in such a rational way...</i>

05:23.406 --> 05:24.991
<i>I can't help but see...</i>

05:27.118 --> 05:29.662
<i>this theory as beautiful!</i>

05:29.746 --> 05:32.165
EARTH

05:32.248 --> 05:35.168
SUN, EARTH

05:36.961 --> 05:39.422
It may... be true.

06:03.237 --> 06:05.740
ORB: ON THE MOVEMENTS OF THE EARTH

07:15.143 --> 07:18.563
Your observations have grown
even more precise lately.

07:19.522 --> 07:20.773
Did something change?

07:26.696 --> 07:27.530
If I may.

07:30.199 --> 07:32.076
Hubert,

07:32.160 --> 07:33.744
why put yourself in danger

07:34.579 --> 07:37.540
and give up your place in heaven
just for this?

07:38.833 --> 07:41.085
Do you want to deny the existence of God?

07:41.586 --> 07:42.670
It's the opposite.

07:43.713 --> 07:45.756
I do it because I believe in God.

07:49.260 --> 07:50.428
Most people believe

07:50.928 --> 07:54.265
this world is an ugly place
filled with greed and corruption,

07:54.348 --> 07:56.893
while the afterlife is pure and beautiful.

07:57.518 --> 07:58.394
But

07:59.103 --> 08:01.272
I can't accept that.

08:02.648 --> 08:04.609
This world created by God

08:05.401 --> 08:07.528
is surely the most beautiful of all.

08:11.115 --> 08:15.244
A person doesn't need
faith, money, or status to know that.

08:16.412 --> 08:18.456
I will show

08:18.539 --> 08:21.083
that even trapped in this tiny skull,

08:21.584 --> 08:24.170
my intellect is all I need
to understand God's works.

08:25.296 --> 08:28.466
That's why I don't read
the holy scripture.

08:28.549 --> 08:29.884
I read nature.

08:32.094 --> 08:34.972
But doesn't a life like that...

08:36.766 --> 08:38.434
frighten you?

08:39.268 --> 08:40.186
It does.

08:42.688 --> 08:43.606
Even so,

08:44.106 --> 08:47.610
a life that isn't frightening
is missing its essence.

08:52.073 --> 08:54.492
Oh, and one more thing.

08:54.575 --> 08:56.786
This is your last day of observation.

08:57.578 --> 08:58.496
What?

09:00.498 --> 09:03.000
I've discovered a way to continue alone.

09:03.626 --> 09:07.547
Then what do I do from tomorrow?

09:09.131 --> 09:11.842
Good question. You're free to choose.

09:12.927 --> 09:14.136
However,

09:14.845 --> 09:15.972
continue astronomy.

09:16.472 --> 09:17.807
For your own sake.

09:21.519 --> 09:23.646
Though that's just a suggestion.

09:25.231 --> 09:27.650
Well, thank you for everything.

09:36.409 --> 09:37.410
<i>It's over.</i>

09:37.910 --> 09:38.911
<i>Just like that.</i>

09:39.745 --> 09:41.330
<i>What was this all about?</i>

09:41.831 --> 09:43.499
<i>"Continue astronomy," he says?</i>

09:43.583 --> 09:45.293
<i>I can't do that.</i>

09:50.047 --> 09:52.466
Potocki? Why is he in front of the house?

09:54.010 --> 09:55.094
Hi!

09:56.679 --> 09:57.680
Huh?

09:59.181 --> 10:00.349
Hello there.

10:05.229 --> 10:07.023
Are you Rafal?

10:07.523 --> 10:09.942
I'm the Inquisitor, Nowak.

10:10.860 --> 10:14.363
I'm here to inquire about Hubert's actions
since his recantation.

10:15.364 --> 10:16.824
I-Is that so?

10:17.325 --> 10:21.162
Hubert has fully reformed,
and he's been living modestly.

10:21.829 --> 10:23.664
Oh? I'm glad to hear that.

10:24.373 --> 10:29.128
After all, a man charged
as a heretic twice will be put to death.

10:29.629 --> 10:32.340
His collaborators
would face serious charges too.

10:32.423 --> 10:35.426
All that extra work
is no fun for me either.

10:35.926 --> 10:37.845
Th-That sounds rough.

10:37.928 --> 10:40.264
I can't tolerate those foolish heretics.

10:40.348 --> 10:42.224
Glad to have your support.

10:44.268 --> 10:45.353
So tell me then...

10:48.189 --> 10:49.315
What's this?

10:51.692 --> 10:53.861
I found it in your bookcase.

10:54.487 --> 10:56.822
I haven't told Potocki yet,

10:57.406 --> 11:01.744
but it sure seems to contain
detailed notes about blasphemous research.

11:02.787 --> 11:03.829
What is this?

11:03.913 --> 11:05.915
It's... uh...

11:07.291 --> 11:09.085
What could it be?

11:11.462 --> 11:13.089
That belongs to me.

11:14.882 --> 11:16.592
H-Hubert?!

11:17.093 --> 11:21.097
I thought it would be harder to find
if I hid it in that child's room,

11:22.056 --> 11:24.266
but it seems I've been caught.

11:24.850 --> 11:28.020
Oh? So that's the case, is it?

11:28.729 --> 11:32.274
But you'd better think carefully, Hubert.

11:32.358 --> 11:33.567
Do you realize

11:33.651 --> 11:37.113
where such a statement will lead you?

11:40.324 --> 11:43.369
I came back to finish what I started.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.415
Be honest, please.

11:47.498 --> 11:50.751
Does this really belong to you?

11:51.919 --> 11:54.046
Of course it does.

11:54.755 --> 11:57.717
In fact, you're the one
who should think carefully.

11:58.384 --> 12:02.263
Do you really think a child
could assist with my research?

12:04.140 --> 12:06.809
Well, I suppose that's true.

12:06.892 --> 12:08.894
Sorry about that, Rafal.

12:11.188 --> 12:14.066
- In that case, put Hubert under arrest.
- Huh?

12:14.734 --> 12:17.069
Wait!

12:17.153 --> 12:18.696
So suddenly?!

12:19.739 --> 12:20.990
Oh, that's right.

12:22.867 --> 12:25.119
I came to give you this.

12:30.249 --> 12:31.667
- Farewell.
- Huh?

12:33.043 --> 12:34.003
Hubert!

12:35.129 --> 12:37.715
Will you really just go?

12:38.215 --> 12:40.134
Weren't you going to finish something?

12:43.971 --> 12:45.389
I just did.

12:52.980 --> 12:54.732
<i>And so, Hubert</i>

12:55.232 --> 12:56.525
<i>was burned to death.</i>

13:00.029 --> 13:02.072
ORB: ON THE MOVEMENTS OF THE EARTH

13:02.156 --> 13:02.990
<i>- Orb.
- Orb.</i>

13:11.916 --> 13:12.833
<i>He died.</i>

13:13.334 --> 13:14.752
<i>To save me.</i>

13:16.170 --> 13:17.963
<i>I know he was a heretic,</i>

13:18.631 --> 13:21.133
<i>but what was the right thing for me to do?</i>

13:22.384 --> 13:24.136
<i>His unfinished work...</i>

13:25.554 --> 13:27.056
Three stars.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.226
Orion's Belt?

13:31.143 --> 13:34.021
Why is only Alnilam
in the center painted black?

13:36.232 --> 13:37.233
I'm fond of the way

13:37.733 --> 13:42.988
those mountains
and rocks resemble Orion's Belt.

13:43.948 --> 13:44.782
Wait!

14:05.803 --> 14:09.139
I've come to the mountain
that represents Alnilam,

14:09.223 --> 14:10.641
but I don't see--

14:28.492 --> 14:29.910
This is

14:30.786 --> 14:31.745
a letter?

14:33.581 --> 14:36.417
"To the person who finds this letter."

14:37.251 --> 14:39.879
<i>Please forgive the curt opening,</i>

14:40.379 --> 14:42.756
<i>but I have no idea who you are.</i>

14:43.257 --> 14:46.927
<i>However, I have decided
to entrust my necklace</i>

14:47.011 --> 14:49.263
<i>to the one I deem most trustworthy.</i>

14:50.890 --> 14:52.683
<i>Now to the main order of business.</i>

14:53.267 --> 14:56.520
<i>The documents you see here
comprise my lifetime of research</i>

14:56.604 --> 14:58.272
<i>into heliocentrism.</i>

14:59.815 --> 15:02.443
<i>I now place all my trust in you</i>

15:03.110 --> 15:05.696
<i>and beg you to finish what I started.</i>

15:06.864 --> 15:07.948
<i>Please,</i>

15:08.032 --> 15:10.159
<i>burn everything.</i>

15:11.994 --> 15:16.040
<i>I am confident that I have spent more time
with heliocentrism than anyone else.</i>

15:16.540 --> 15:17.791
<i>Because of that,</i>

15:17.875 --> 15:20.336
<i>there is something I alone know.</i>

15:20.419 --> 15:22.004
SUN, EARTH

15:22.087 --> 15:24.381
<i>Heliocentrism can likely never be proven.</i>

15:25.925 --> 15:28.135
<i>There are too many uncertain factors.</i>

15:29.178 --> 15:30.220
<i>It surely must be</i>

15:30.304 --> 15:32.723
<i>the realm of God himself.</i>

15:33.390 --> 15:34.892
<i>If that is the case,</i>

15:34.975 --> 15:37.561
<i>such an imperfect theory should disappear.</i>

15:39.480 --> 15:41.649
<i>Despite that, I don't have the will</i>

15:41.732 --> 15:43.484
<i>or the courage to burn it myself.</i>

15:43.984 --> 15:45.653
<i>Instead, it is my selfish hope</i>

15:45.736 --> 15:49.531
<i>that someone superior to me
will dispose of it forever.</i>

15:51.742 --> 15:52.910
<i>That is you.</i>

15:54.453 --> 15:56.163
<i>You are capable of burning it.</i>

15:56.872 --> 16:01.001
<i>Your powers of reason
are far stronger than my intuition.</i>

16:01.669 --> 16:03.128
<i>You can do it.</i>

16:04.213 --> 16:06.507
<i>A reward for the task
can be found in the box.</i>

16:07.007 --> 16:08.717
<i>The amount should be sufficient.</i>

16:11.053 --> 16:13.013
<i>And so, I leave it to you.</i>

16:16.976 --> 16:19.019
<i>Well, it is what it is.</i>

16:20.062 --> 16:23.023
<i>I understand why he chose
to leave this letter too.</i>

16:24.233 --> 16:26.735
<i>Heliocentrism is indeed an amazing idea.</i>

16:27.569 --> 16:30.614
<i>But it's too dangerous,
too out of step with the times,</i>

16:31.699 --> 16:33.951
<i>and more than anything else,
too uncertain.</i>

16:34.994 --> 16:37.371
<i>This is the most reasonable outcome.</i>

16:38.372 --> 16:39.957
<i>The materials must be burned.</i>

16:41.542 --> 16:43.210
<i>It's just as Hubert said.</i>

16:45.087 --> 16:46.630
<i>My powers of reason</i>

16:46.714 --> 16:48.257
<i>set the documents aflame.</i>

16:57.850 --> 16:58.684
<i>But...</i>

17:04.523 --> 17:05.774
Ow!

17:07.568 --> 17:09.361
More than that reasoning,

17:09.945 --> 17:13.115
my intuition wants to believe
in heliocentrism!

17:17.411 --> 17:19.038
Everyone, listen up!

17:19.121 --> 17:23.876
While we're sorry to see him go,
today is the day Rafal leaves our school!

17:23.959 --> 17:24.793
However,

17:25.753 --> 17:27.671
he'll be attending university.

17:28.338 --> 17:29.465
And everyone,

17:29.548 --> 17:32.134
what is the most appropriate field
for him to study?

17:32.760 --> 17:34.094
Do you remember?

17:34.678 --> 17:36.513
- Theology!
- Theology!

17:36.597 --> 17:37.681
That's right.

17:38.182 --> 17:41.393
Rafal, do you have any parting words?

17:41.477 --> 17:42.311
Yes.

17:45.939 --> 17:48.108
Thank you for all you've done for me.

17:48.609 --> 17:50.486
We won't see each other anymore,

17:50.569 --> 17:53.739
but I pray that you receive
God's blessings.

17:55.074 --> 17:56.283
Oh, and one more thing.

17:58.952 --> 18:01.246
I'm going to study astronomy.

18:05.292 --> 18:08.712
<i>Though it pains me to say it,
the world is full of fools.</i>

18:09.797 --> 18:13.550
<i>And before I knew it,
I was at the head of the line.</i>

18:17.054 --> 18:18.222
<i>The real me</i>

18:18.722 --> 18:22.476
<i>is neither dignified,
nor wise, humble, or capable.</i>

18:22.559 --> 18:25.104
<i>What I am is arrogant, brazen,</i>

18:25.187 --> 18:26.980
<i>rash, and helpless.</i>

18:27.773 --> 18:30.943
<i>And now... I'm going to move the Earth.</i>

18:39.493 --> 18:41.620
If you need help, just ask an adult.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.499
See? Just like that.

18:49.253 --> 18:50.379
Here you go.

18:50.462 --> 18:51.880
Thank you very much!

18:51.964 --> 18:55.175
I can't just ignore a crying child.

18:55.676 --> 18:57.386
Be good to your family, okay?

18:58.554 --> 18:59.388
Yes, sir!

19:00.514 --> 19:02.307
Nowak, we'd better get moving.

19:02.891 --> 19:05.018
Huh? Oh, right.

19:08.897 --> 19:12.151
I hope you'll forgive the sudden visit.

19:14.987 --> 19:17.030
What do you intend to do?

19:17.823 --> 19:19.199
I have a child!

19:20.159 --> 19:24.037
Oh, is that so? I have a daughter myself.

19:24.121 --> 19:28.292
She just turned four,
and she's quite cute.

19:30.627 --> 19:33.130
Look, this is a letter from my daughter.

19:33.213 --> 19:35.674
I always carry it with me.

19:37.759 --> 19:40.554
Whenever I think of her,
I get the same feelings.

19:41.263 --> 19:44.141
Comfort, strength, and...

19:45.767 --> 19:47.019
worry.

19:48.270 --> 19:51.481
Love for my child
has become my reason to live.

19:52.232 --> 19:54.943
I don't ever want her to suffer.

19:55.986 --> 20:00.574
So any research that will disrupt
the peace can't be overlooked.

20:02.242 --> 20:07.206
To tell the truth, I don't have
any lofty ideals like protecting humanity.

20:07.706 --> 20:10.500
But when it comes to protecting
the lives and faith

20:10.584 --> 20:13.837
of my family and friends,

20:14.838 --> 20:16.423
there's nothing I won't do.

20:19.468 --> 20:21.220
I'm home!

20:23.972 --> 20:25.265
Oh, my.

20:25.349 --> 20:27.809
So this was your family.

20:36.693 --> 20:39.571
Okay, this is where the wicked gather.

20:39.655 --> 20:41.156
I'll leave the rest to you.

20:41.657 --> 20:43.825
I have dinner with my family to get to.

20:43.909 --> 20:44.910
Huh?

20:44.993 --> 20:47.371
Aren't inquisitors celibate too?

20:47.454 --> 20:49.122
You didn't know?

20:49.206 --> 20:51.959
Nowak never joined the clergy.
He's a layperson.

20:52.459 --> 20:53.669
I don't know the details,

20:53.752 --> 20:57.631
but the Bishop thinks highly of him
and made an exception.

20:57.714 --> 20:59.383
He was once a mercenary.

20:59.466 --> 21:01.093
A mercenary?

21:01.176 --> 21:03.845
How could such bloody hands
do the Lord's work?

21:04.346 --> 21:05.597
It's unthinkable.

21:06.556 --> 21:08.433
How could this be?

21:09.434 --> 21:11.270
Don't get so disheartened.

21:11.770 --> 21:14.064
I'm sure the Bishop has his reasons.

21:15.941 --> 21:17.359
You must

21:18.026 --> 21:19.278
be joking.

21:20.946 --> 21:22.614
You're joking, right?

21:25.075 --> 21:26.076
Huh?

21:28.161 --> 21:32.749
Not only are you abandoning theology,
but it's to study astronomy?

21:34.418 --> 21:37.546
Has Hubert being arrested as a heretic

21:37.629 --> 21:39.756
momentarily robbed you of your senses?

21:42.384 --> 21:44.636
If you don't retract that statement,

21:44.720 --> 21:48.015
I won't sign
this university admission form!

21:52.185 --> 21:53.687
<i>Recently,</i>

21:54.396 --> 21:57.774
<i>after my sudden change in direction,</i>

21:57.858 --> 22:01.069
<i>my future has grown quite precarious.</i>

22:02.821 --> 22:04.656
<i>Being honest,</i>

22:04.740 --> 22:06.366
<i>skillfully explaining myself,</i>

22:06.450 --> 22:09.202
<i>and settling all concerns
would be a Herculean task.</i>

22:12.622 --> 22:14.249
Now, declare it!

22:15.000 --> 22:16.918
You won't study astronomy!

22:18.253 --> 22:19.296
<i>And so...</i>

22:20.589 --> 22:22.799
Understood. I declare it.

22:23.592 --> 22:25.552
I'll never study astronomy again.

22:26.511 --> 22:28.138
<i>...I simply lied.</i>

22:28.764 --> 22:33.226
Oh, my son!
You've returned to your normal self?

22:33.310 --> 22:35.520
Yes! I was being a fool!

22:36.021 --> 22:37.689
I'm so happy!

22:38.523 --> 22:40.484
<i>One can express anything in words.</i>

22:40.984 --> 22:42.778
<i>That's why lying is so convenient.</i>

22:44.363 --> 22:47.074
<i>The rational judgment I've developed</i>

22:47.574 --> 22:49.576
<i>can help me avoid trouble.</i>

22:53.914 --> 22:55.707
<i>Right. That's the way.</i>

22:56.666 --> 22:58.543
<i>Even if I enroll in theology,</i>

22:58.627 --> 23:00.629
<i>I can transfer to astronomy later.</i>

23:01.421 --> 23:04.841
<i>Not going to university
would defeat the purpose.</i>

23:06.301 --> 23:08.428
<i>Proving heliocentrism</i>

23:08.929 --> 23:11.056
<i>could take 30 or 40 years.</i>

23:11.932 --> 23:14.267
<i>But even then, it's no pipe dream.</i>

23:14.768 --> 23:17.729
<i>I just need to proceed little by little.</i>

23:19.314 --> 23:20.774
<i>Still,</i>

23:20.857 --> 23:23.985
<i>if my father hates astronomy so much,</i>

23:25.445 --> 23:29.199
<i>why are there so many
books on it inside this house?</i>

24:56.995 --> 25:00.999
Subtitle translation by: Brad Plumb
